====================================================================================================
(E) closed form for the odd numbers.  N_d = d exactly, so
      Gamma^(q)(odds) = 1 + SUM_d [q^d + (1-q)^d] = 1 + q/(1-q) + (1-q)/q
                      = 1/(q(1-q)) - 1,   minimised at q=1/2 with value 3.
====================================================================================================
      q   Gamma^(q) summed   1/(q(1-q)) - 1       diff
   0.10       10.111111111     10.111111111   5.33e-15
   0.20        5.250000000      5.250000000   8.88e-16
   0.25        4.333333333      4.333333333   8.88e-16
   0.30        3.761904762      3.761904762   1.33e-15
   0.40        3.166666667      3.166666667   2.66e-15
   0.50        3.000000000      3.000000000   0.00e+00
   0.60        3.166666667      3.166666667   2.66e-15
   0.70        3.761904762      3.761904762   1.33e-15
   0.80        5.250000000      5.250000000   2.66e-15
  q(1-q) <= 1/4 always, so Gamma^(q)(odds) >= 3 with equality only at q = 1/2:
  the fair coin gives the LEAST rugged landscape of the odd numbers.
